The prompt must be in English, comma-separated keywords/phrases format optimized for text-to-image generation.
Include ALL of the following elements:
- Subject: the main subject, actions, and objects in the scene — make it specific to the topic
- Style: artistic medium and visual style (digital painting, concept art, photograph, illustration, 3D render, cinematic, etc.)
- Lighting: light source and quality (golden hour, dramatic side lighting, soft diffused light, rim light, studio lighting, volumetric, etc.)
- Colors: dominant color palette and harmony (vibrant, pastel, monochrome, warm tones, cool tones, complementary, analogous, etc.)
- Composition: framing and perspective (close-up, wide shot, bird's eye view, rule of thirds, leading lines, depth of field, etc.)
- Mood: emotional atmosphere (serene, energetic, mysterious, cinematic, cozy, majestic, dramatic, futuristic, etc.)

Start with the subject: who is doing what, with which objects, in the first ~15 words.
Name concrete, drawable things (a person, a tool, a stack of papers, a clock) — never
abstract nouns like "cost", "efficiency", "value". Put quality and style tags at the END.

Each image index represents a different visual angle or aspect of the topic. Vary the prompts across images — do NOT repeat the same template or phrasing between different indices.

The image must contain no text, no letters, no captions, no interface labels.

Return ONLY the comma-separated prompt text. No explanations, no markdown formatting.
